# === Vercel example — local config, DO NOT COMMIT with your values ===
# Usage:
#   cp deploy-examples/vercel.example .deploy.local   (then fill in the URL below)
#   npm run package                                    (build + ZIP)
#
# Notes:
# - Normal deploy: import the repo on vercel.com (vercel.json already
#   runs the build). Vercel does NOT accept ZIPs: the ZIP is only an archive
#   or for a generic host.
# - IP counter: single Worker+D1 backend recommended (see IPS.md) —
#   fill in HUGO_VISIT_API_URL below. Without it, deprecated Vercel KV
#   fallback (Storage > Create Database > KV linked to the project).
# - VERCEL_TOKEN: only useful for the Vercel CLI/API, not for the ZIP.

# Target platform (do not change in this file)
TARGET=vercel

# Final public URL — REQUIRED (Vercel domain or custom domain):
# https://mon-site.vercel.app  |  https://www.mon-domaine.fr
SITE_URL=https://mon-site.vercel.app

# --- Single visits/IP backend (optional, see IPS.md) ---
# HUGO_VISIT_API_URL=https://mon-licenciement-visits.<account>.workers.dev/api/visit

# --- SEO: verification + IndexNow (optional, see DEPLOY.md SEO section) ---
# HUGO_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=
# HUGO_BING_SITE_VERIFICATION=
# INDEXNOW_KEY= (generate via npm run seo:init)

# --- Giscus comments (optional, see COMMENTAIRES.md) ---
# Uncomment and fill in the 4 values copied from https://giscus.app
# GISCUS_REPO=USER/REPO
# GISCUS_REPO_ID=R_xxx
# GISCUS_CATEGORY=Announcements
# GISCUS_CATEGORY_ID=DIC_xxx

# --- API token (optional, Vercel CLI only) ---
# VERCEL_TOKEN=
